0..82 Comment "//! The folds over a polymorphic list — its length, appending and mapping — in"
83..159 Comment "//! the spellings an arm admits, each as the sugared form writes it: a `run`"
160..238 Comment "//! that only sequences a call, its result returned or the `return` elided, is"
239..315 Comment "//! written with the call nested in the constructor it returns. A structural"
316..383 Comment "//! recursive call stands one stage below the list it was read from"
384..464 Comment "//! [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]; the list is the polymorphic one"
465..543 Comment "//! of Martin-Löf\'s type theory. A fold may take the element type implicitly,"
544..621 Comment "//! `[a : Type]`: its recursive call omits `a` and passes the function\'s own."
622..682 Comment "//! They run at the naturals in `recursive-nat-lists.gandr`."
683..686 Comment "//!"
687..743 Comment "//! - cites: [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]"
744..747 Comment "//!"
748..872 Comment "//! [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]: https://doi.org/10.1051/ita:2004015 \"Abel, Termination checking with types\""
874..904 Comment "// The naturals and the lists."
